//// Decisions 120 and 121 of 1.0.10-beta (front 24, § Cells "`@Task` and
//// failure") — a Task never fails: `throw` needs a `@Result` in some layer of
//// the return, and `@Task<i32>` has none. Refused at the `throw`.
////
//// Line 1 is the shared tail of the code on purpose: the README's table names
//// `effect-try-without-fallible-channel` for `throw` and `try` alike, while the
//// checker at `82e32e36` answers a `throw` with
//// `effect-throw-without-fallible-channel` — whether the two merge is the
//// README's open point 2, and this cell holds either answer.

fn answer(n: i32) -> @Task<i32> {
    if (n < 0) { throw "negative"; };
    return n;
}

pub fn main() { answer(1); }
